<article class="script-document" aria-labelledby="calling-script-title">
<div class="script-dialog-header"><div><small>TALKVIA · AGENT GUIDE</small><h2 id="calling-script-title">Klu Care calling script</h2></div><span class="badge">Klu Care · Sales</span></div>
<div class="script-dialog-body">
<p class="script-intro">Use this as a conversation guide. Replace bracketed words with the correct details.</p>
<details open><summary>1. Reception / gatekeeper</summary><p>“Hi, good morning. This is [Agent Name] from Talkvia, calling regarding Klu Care, a hospital management software. Could you please connect me with the person responsible for evaluating your hospital’s management software? Would that be your administrator, operations manager or IT manager?”</p><p><strong>If asked what this is regarding:</strong> “We’d like to understand whether your hospital is reviewing its current software and whether a demonstration of Klu Care would be relevant.”</p><p><strong>If referred to another number:</strong> “Thank you. May I confirm the number, the person’s name and their job title? I’ll contact them directly.”</p><p><strong>If unavailable:</strong> “Could I have their name and job title, please? What would be a convenient time to reach them?”</p></details>
<details open><summary>2. Decision-maker opening</summary><p>“Hi [Name], this is [Agent Name] from Talkvia, calling regarding Klu Care, a hospital management software. Have I caught you at a convenient time for a brief introduction?”</p><p>“Thank you. Before I explain further, may I ask what system you currently use to manage your hospital’s day-to-day operations?”</p></details>
<details open><summary>3. Understand their requirements</summary><p>“Is your current system meeting your needs, or are there areas you would like to improve?”</p><p>“What is the biggest challenge your team faces with the current setup?”</p><p>“Are you considering a software change, or exploring options for the future?”</p><p><strong>If they mention a requirement:</strong> “Thank you—that helps. I’ll note that requirement so the Klu Care team can address it and confirm whether the software is suitable for your workflow.”</p></details>
<details open><summary>4. Offer a demo and confirm details</summary><p>“Based on what you’ve shared, would you be open to a demonstration of Klu Care? You could review the software, discuss your requirements and decide whether it would be a suitable fit.”</p><p>“What date and time would work best for you? Just to confirm, that is [Date] at [Time] in your local timezone, correct?”</p><p>“Could you please confirm your full name, job title and the best email address for the demonstration details?”</p><p>“Will anyone else be involved in evaluating the software who should join the discussion?”</p></details>
<details open><summary>5. “We already have software”</summary><p>“Understood. Is it working well for your team, or is there anything you wish it handled better?”</p><p><strong>If satisfied:</strong> “That’s good to hear. Would you like a brief introduction by email for future reference?”</p></details>
<details open><summary>6. “Send me an email” / “Call later”</summary><p><strong>Email:</strong> “Certainly. What is the best email address to use? Is there a particular requirement you would like the information to address? Would you prefer to contact us if interested, or may I follow up at a convenient time?”</p><p><strong>Callback:</strong> “Of course. What date and time would suit you, in your local timezone? Thank you. I’ll note [Date, Time and Timezone]. Should I ask for you directly, and is this the best number to reach you?”</p></details>
<details open><summary>7. Pricing, features and integrations</summary><p><strong>Pricing:</strong> “I don’t want to give you an inaccurate figure. I can arrange for the Klu Care team to confirm pricing based on your requirements. Would you prefer that by email or during a discussion?”</p><p><strong>Feature / integration / compliance question:</strong> “I’ll note that question and have the product team confirm it accurately. Could you tell me a little more about what you need?”</p></details>
<details open><summary>8. Not interested / do not call</summary><p><strong>Not interested:</strong> “Understood. Thank you for your time. Have a good day.”</p><p><strong>Do not call:</strong> “Certainly. I’ll record your request not to receive further calls. Thank you.”</p></details>
<details open><summary>9. Confirm and close</summary><p>“Thank you, [Name]. To confirm, your main requirement is [Requirement], and the next step is [Demo / Email / Callback] on [Date] at [Hospital Local Time and Timezone]. We have your email as [Email Address]. Is that correct? Thank you for your time. Have a great day.”</p></details>
<details open><summary>10. Voicemail</summary><p>“Hello [Name], this is [Agent Name] from Talkvia, calling regarding Klu Care, a hospital management software. We’d welcome the opportunity to understand your requirements and see whether a demonstration would be useful. You can reach us at [Approved Callback Number]. Thank you.”</p></details>
<div class="script-agent-note"><strong>After each call</strong><p>Check Number dialed, source name/title, notes and outcome. If referred, select Referred to Another Number, enter the new Callback number and note who referred you. Check Number dialed reflects the call you just made. Use Save call &amp; stay for intermediate calls at this hospital; use Dispose &amp; next hospital for the final call. Enter callbacks/demos in the hospital’s local timezone. Make only confirmed product/pricing claims.</p></div>
</div></article>
